WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.600
Release day, ten a.m.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.300
The pipeline is stuck,
the alerts are on,

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.900
and a whole team is waiting
on one deploy.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.000
I've spent five years making sure
that moment never comes.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.950
I'm Adrien, a freelance full-stack
and platform engineer from Paris,

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.800
working remotely across Europe.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.350
I build the platforms other
engineers ship on,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.700
so your team ships on time,
and goes home on time.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.100
No surprises. No late nights.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.000
The proof is in the systems.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.100
At Thales Alenia Space,

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.750
I parallelised satellite image compression
across eighty cores.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.100
At Schneider Electric, in Boston,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.250
I shipped Go and Python micro-apps
to industrial edge devices,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.900
with observability built in.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.300
Today at Criteo, I build the continuous
deployment platform

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.300
that fifteen hundred engineers
use every day.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.000
And SignalAtlas is my own product:

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.400
I designed, built and run it,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.600
from first commit to production.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.100
But code is only half the job.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.250
I demo every week, write updates
you can forward,

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.950
and leave a runbook your team
can run without me.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.850
I train and mentor the
engineers around me,

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.800
in English or in French.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.950
I use AI agents daily,

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.800
and I review and own every
line that ships.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.700
Tell me about your mission.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.350
My email and portfolio
are on screen,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.600
and the first call is free.

